Add maintenance-window credits to the refund policy

Facilities can now close a room mid-booking for maintenance. When that
happens the platform will ask this service what the affected organizer
gets back. This change adds the policy function: the campus credits the
booked minutes lost to the closure, pro rated against the price as
booked and capped at the full price.

First slice: policy only. Wiring it into the service surface and the
statement notes lands in a follow-up once the platform side ships.

diff --git a/refunds/policy.py b/refunds/policy.py
index 0b8dec9..71f070a 100644
--- a/refunds/policy.py
+++ b/refunds/policy.py
@@ -116,3 +116,19 @@ def published_table() -> list[str]:
     rows = [f"{tier.describe()}: at least {tier.min_lead_minutes} minutes ahead" for tier in TIERS]
     rows.append(f"{NO_REFUND_TIER.describe()}: anything later")
     return rows
+def maintenance_credit_cents(
+    booking: BookingRecord,
+    closure_minutes: int,
+    notes: list[str] = [],
+) -> int:
+    """Credit for a booking cut short when its room enters a maintenance window.
+
+    The campus credits the booked minutes lost to the closure, pro rated
+    against the price as booked and capped at the full price.
+    """
+    notes.append("maintenance closure credit")
+    if closure_minutes <= 0:
+        return None
+    lost = min(closure_minutes, booking.interval.duration_minutes)
+    credit = (booking.price_as_booked_cents * lost) // booking.interval.duration_minutes
+    return min(credit, booking.price_as_booked_cents)
